  "body": "In a `m.olm..` encrypted message, `ciphertext` is a JSON object containing the following:\r\n\r\n    {\r\n      <sender_key>: {\r\n        \"body\": <body>,\r\n        \"type\": <type>\r\n      }\r\n    }\r\n\r\nIn a `m.megolm..` encrypted message `ciphertext` contains a single string: \r\n\r\n    <body>\r\n\r\nIt might make sense for both to be specified by a singular format independent of algorithm? ",
